{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Like the green herb I have given you everything.</b> From the fact that He mentioned 'I have given you everything,' I would have thought that all flesh is permitted, as per the opinion of the nations; therefore He needed to say 'like the green herb' — just as among herbs there is a permitted portion, namely those that are good and beneficial, and a forbidden portion, namely those that are harmful and deadly, so too among living creatures there is a permitted portion, which is what the Torah permitted, and a forbidden portion, which is what the Torah forbade. And this is the correct sense of the verse (peshat), for the verse did not come to permit all flesh." "<b>And our Rabbis of blessed memory</b> interpreted: 'Like the green herb' — which I gave to the first man and I did not permit him flesh; 'I have given you everything' — I have permitted you everything, even flesh. For all flesh had incurred annihilation in the Flood, and by their merit they were saved; therefore I am permitting you to slaughter and eat."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:21.187386631Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}